  "readme": "## README.md\n# Open Climate Risk\n\nThis Source Cooperative repository contains data products for the [Open Climate Risk](https://carbonplan.org/research/climate-risk) project. These data were used to build a scalable pipeline for calculating climate risk assessments at building-level resolution across the continental United States. Wildfire risk was calculated through a distributed processing system that can run locally or on cloud infrastructure. Technical documentation can be found [here](https://docs.carbonplan.org/ocr).\n\n## Working with the data\nDocumentation for working with the raster and vector data can be found [here](https://docs.carbonplan.org/ocr/en/latest/how-to/work-with-data.html).\n\n## Data Formats\n\n**Tensor** \n- Our raw input data consisted of either Zarr or TIFF files. We processed it into rechunked Icechunk stores. \n- Our n-dimensional output data is stored as a single Icechunk store. \n\n**Vector**\n- Our raw input data was either GPKG or Geoparquet. All the vector pipeline inputs were converted to Geoparquet.\n- Our output vector data is stored in multiple formats. See [our documentation on data access](https://docs.carbonplan.org/ocr/en/latest/access-data.html) for more details.\n    - Hive-partitioned (state/county) Geoparquet file for risk sampled buildings across CONUS. \n    - PMTiles layers for buildings, Census blocks, Census Tracts and counties.\n    - Summary statistics files in GPKG and CSV\n\n## Data structure\n\nThe data is split into `inputs` and `outputs,` where `inputs` are raw and processed data for the pipeline, and `outputs` are versioned dataset outputs.\n\n```bash\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 input\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 fire-risk\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 tensor\n\u2502       \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 USFS (Icechunk & TIFF)\n\u2502       \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 dillon-et-al-2023 \n\u2502       \u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 riley-et-al-2025 \n\u2502       \u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 scott-et-al-2024 \n\u2502       \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 conus404-ffwi (Icechunk)\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 vector\n\u2502           \u251c\u2500\u2500 census-tiger (Geoparquet)\n\u2502           \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 LICENSE.txt (CC BY 4.0) \n\u2502           \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 blocks \n\u2502           \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 counties\n\u2502           \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 tracts\n\u2502           \u2514\u2500\u2500 overture-maps (Geoparquet)\n\u2502                \u2514\u2500\u2500 LICENSE.txt (ODbL)\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 output\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 fire-risk\n        \u251c\u2500\u2500 tensor (Icechunk)\n        \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 LICENSE.txt (CC BY 4.0)\n        \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 NOTICE.txt\n        \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 production\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500 vector (Geoparquet, PMTiles, GPKG, csv)\n            \u251c\u2500\u2500 LICENSE.txt (ODbL)\n            \u251c\u2500\u2500 NOTICE.txt\n            \u2514\u2500\u2500 production\n\n```\n\n## Data Sources\n\nThe tensor outputs rely on data from [K Riley et al. 2025](https://doi.org/10.2737/RDS-2025-0006), [J Scott et al. 2024](https://doi.org/10.2737/RDS-2020-0016-2), and [R Rasmussen et al. 2023](https://doi.org/10.1175/BAMS-D-21-0326.1). The vector outputs additionally incorporate data from the [Overture Maps Foundation buildings dataset](https://docs.overturemaps.org/guides/buildings/) and [Census TIGER/Line](https://www.census.gov/geographies/mapping-files/time-series/geo/tiger-line-file.html). Read more about our data sources [here](https://docs.carbonplan.org/ocr/en/latest/reference/data-sources.html). \n\n\n## Terms of use\n\nBy viewing Open Climate Risk data, you agree to CarbonPlan\u2019s [Terms of Use](https://carbonplan.org/terms) and [Privacy Policy](https://carbonplan.org/privacy).\n\nThis work contains information from the Overture Maps buildings database, which is made available here under the [Open Database License](https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl) (ODbL).\n\nLicenses for tensor ([CC BY 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0)) and vector ([ODbL](https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0)) data are packaged with the data in colocated LICENSE.txt files.",
